  "goodToKnow": "Der Rettungswagen (RTW) is an ambulance, called via 112, the number for fire and ambulance (110 is the police). Everyday speech also uses der Krankenwagen. In a traffic jam on the Autobahn, drivers must form a Rettungsgasse (emergency corridor) between the far-left lane and the others; not doing so can be fined. The plural is the same: die Rettungswagen."
